<p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">30.43%</span></p></td><td class=\"px-sm py-xs leading-5 border-sm border-solid border-neutral-border relative\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; width: 75px; vertical-align: top;\"><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">17.39%</span></p></td><td class=\"px-sm py-xs leading-5 border-sm border-solid border-neutral-border relative\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; width: 75px; vertical-align: top;\"><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">17.39%</span></p></td><td class=\"px-sm py-xs leading-5 border-sm border-solid border-neutral-border relative\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; width: 75px; vertical-align: top;\"><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">34.78%</span></p></td><td class=\"px-sm py-xs leading-5 border-sm border-solid border-neutral-border relative\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; width: 75px; vertical-align: top;\"><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">0%</span></p></td><td class=\"px-sm py-xs leading-5 border-sm border-solid border-neutral-border relative\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; width: 75px; vertical-align: top;\"><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Nazibol1234 +4.35</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The polls with lower sample sizes in this instance are probably made up of more active voters, those who have a VoterID and actually bother to vote. As I stated earlier, turnout in the last election was 16 voters. Turnout on this election’s polls is 18 at its lowest and 35 at its highest, with lower size polls giving wiptes a sizable lead in the first round(as well as Golden Eagle Gallup’s final-round of RCV estimation showing the largest potential landslide in TSR history.)</span></p><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">It seems voter enthusiasm is soaring to the highest highs in 6 months, and all things considered, I would estimate turnout to be around 18 votes. That means wiptes, in my opinion, is set to win the first round comfortably(+20), and potentially reach the territory of the largest percentage of votes in TSR history(&gt;70.4%). If turnout attacks 25 or higher (unlikely to happen in my opinion), there might be a closer first round and RCV will do the rest.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Probabilities coming soon.</span></p><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Watch out for possible per-group data on the TSRElects webpage: </span><a href=\"https://pickleartgeek.github.io/wikiElectionsResults/\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">https://pickleartgeek.github.io/wikiElectionsResults/</span></a></p><p class=\"first:mt-0 last:mb-0\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Also look out for new BaseCalc polling aggregation over at </span><a href=\"https://wikielectionstsr.my.canva.site/basecalc-2\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">https://wikielectionstsr.my.canva.site/basecalc-2</span></a></p></div>",
